<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vratislaus II of Bohemia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1032–1092</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Vratislav II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vratislaus II was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> from 1061 and the first Bohemian ruler to hold the title of king, granted personally by Emperor Henry IV in 1085 for his support during the Investiture Controversy. He moved his residence to Vyšehrad and founded a chapter there. The royal title was not hereditary and lapsed at his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vratislaus-ii-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="Vratislaus II of Bohemia" width="320" height="514" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous fresco in Znojmo (CZ) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vratislav_II.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
